Compare feedback predictions with published and independent evidence (@engineering-feedback-evidence: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Investigate-feedback-limits-sampling-and-observation-evidence.lingua#r_001F53EF1EF8FC5D84983E0478") { r_007495D7B0A939ABFEED33FBC3
A response model should support a bounded claim about a specified realization. Record the state, interfaces, measured quantity, parameter domain, initial condition, control timing, input limits and excluded dynamics. Keep exact consequences of these premises separate from evidence that a particular physical system satisfies them. Reuse [Connect realization to verification and intended use](Connect-realization-to-verification-and-intended-use.lingua#r_0C593F4A7A204FABB3B5876653), [Keep service evidence meaningful through change and recovery](Keep-service-evidence-meaningful-through-change-and-recovery.lingua#r_0593D3DFF3699AB8D9E3ACE10B) and [Review fitting evidence before extending scientific claims](../../inquiry/core/Review fitting evidence before extending scientific claims.lingua#r_008E6FD7D2B90DB8ED1CE9927E) rather than treating a plotted curve as commissioning evidence.

For a bounded published comparison, use [Process Dynamics Operations and Control MIT 10 450](../sources/Process-Dynamics-Operations-and-Control-MIT-10-450.lingua#r_003D567CD90DDFE67ADB65399E), lesson 3 equations 3.19-2 with the supplied lesson 3.11 values V=6 m³,F=0.02 m³/s and concentrate 400 kg/m³. The open time constant is 300 s. At controller gains 0,0.0001,0.0003,0.0009 m⁶/(kg·s), the dimensionless factors 1+C_Ac K_c/F are 1,3,7,19. Thus the closed time constants are 300,100,300/7,300/19 s, disturbance gains 1,1/3,1/7,1/19 and reference gains 0,2/3,6/7,18/19. This reproduces selected algebraic predictions of the approximate model, not the complete plotted experiment or a physical blending system.

Retain the source approximation: the concentrated stream is small relative to the main flow. Its supplied reference balance gives 8+400(0.0001)/0.02=10 kg/m³ in that approximation; the complete mixed-flow denominator would give 2000/201≈9.95025 kg/m³. The discrepancy is about 0.5%, consistent with its stated within-one-percent observation. Do not silently use the simplified model as exact physical conservation for arbitrary makeup flow.

The original investigation adds its own 100-second unit disturbance pulse to the normalized first-order equations. At effective factors 7 and 19 its peak deviations are(1−exp(−7/3))/7 and(1−exp(−19/3))/19. They fall above and below 0.1 respectively. This pulse duration is an explicit study choice, not a claim that every detail or point in the source's Figure 3.20-1 was reproduced. The source's model parameters and conditional gains are the published comparison; the new pulse is an added test.

For independent computational evidence, use rational enclosures for the exponential. For 0≤x<n, logarithm inequalities ln(1−x/n)≤−x/n≤−ln(1+x/n) yield (1−x/n)^n≤exp(−x)≤(1+x/n)^(−n). The bounds are exact rational values for rational x; increasing n tightens them. They are intentionally wider than 70-digit arithmetic and do not claim 70-digit verification. Affine interval propagation encloses continuous and sampled trajectories; a small extra tolerance covers arithmetic rounding, not physical uncertainty. Exact steady-state formulas are separately checked against rational bisection of the clipped balance.

An acceptance investigation should include a changed reference or disturbance, independently checked input/observation timing, sensor-reference evidence and inspection of residual patterns against plausible alternative models. The structural d+Gb ambiguity requires added information, not merely additional samples. A critic should try to break the claim by changing a boundary, saturating the actuator or adding an omitted delay. Revise the scope in response to evidence. No apparatus validation, laboratory campaign or completed independent learner project is claimed by the programs.

